## Markdown tables

Markdown tables use pipe syntax. A separator row (with `-` characters between pipes) immediately under the header row is required; colons on the separator drive column alignment.

```
| Syntax | Effect |
|:-------|:-------|
| `:---` | left-aligned (default) |
| `:---:` | centre-aligned |
| `---:` | right-aligned |
```

| Syntax | Effect |
|:-------|:-------|
| `:---` | left-aligned (default) |
| `:---:` | centre-aligned |
| `---:` | right-aligned |

Example with mixed alignment and inline emphasis inside cells:

| Left-aligned | Centred | Right-aligned |
|:-------------|:-------:|--------------:|
| *italic*     | **bold** | `code`       |
| ~~struck~~   | one      | two          |
| seven        | eight    | nine         |

Blank lines or any line not starting with `|` end the table. Cell content is parsed as an inline run, so emphasis markers (`*italic*`, `**bold**`, `` `code` `` etc.) fire inside cells.